        "text": "{\"outputs\":{\"result\":{\"type\":\"application/json\",\"data\":{\"graph\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b\",\"revision\":2,\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/04a48ac6-3f02-4dee-8148-7af28470b357.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"review\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Review the first usable planning and review MVP in the app\",\"description\":\"Accept the two surfaces by using them to plan and review real next work.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• User reviews the app against the board/graph references and success criteria.\\n\\n• Plan at least one next task, inspect evidence and complete this review through the new app surface.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. User can plan, persist, inspect and review real work without relying on this temporary document.\\n\\n2. All review comments are closed and required approval/checks pass.\\n\\n3. Deferred refinements are recorded as inputs/tasks; no open blocker is disguised as backlog.\\n\\n4. User explicitly accepts the presented MVP revision.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• In-app review and comment history\\n\\n• User-created/edited next task\\n\\n• Final reviewed revision and checks\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"R03\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"review\":{\"status\":\"draft\",\"reviewers\":[{\"actorId\":\"human:user\",\"required\":true}],\"runnables\":[],\"outcomes\":{},\"target\":null},\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"},{\"id\":\"review\",\"label\":\"Review\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/0aa611cc-79a9-448f-8953-86bb809854a7.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"planning\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Share versioned check tooling across repositories\",\"description\":\"Let Broccoli, templates and other repositories reuse check infrastructure without copying pipelines, preserving exact definition versions and applicability.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Identify reusable parts of the Broccoli testing system and template integration needs.\\n\\n• Design code/API-defined versioned checks/pipelines and choose a linking/pinning approach from evidence; Git submodules are an option, not a decision.\\n\\n• Check/provider-owned applicability predicates with an explicit escape hatch when conventions conflict.\\n\\n• Expose semantic capabilities through portable tools first; avoid dependence on Codex-specific hooks.\\n\\n• Coverage evidence with computed and literal threshold provenance and system/file/function scope for critical code.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. A shared check can serve Broccoli and a template without duplicated test-system implementation.\\n\\n2. Runs identify the exact shared definition revision, target version and applicability reasoning; updates do not rewrite old results.\\n\\n3. A user can force a check where conventions miss it, with the override visible.\\n\\n4. Coverage reports distinguish measured values from thresholds, show how each threshold was obtained or overridden and expose relevant file/function coverage.\\n\\n5. Follow-up scope and implementation are reviewed separately; this task is not a dependency or completion criterion of the current MVP.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Reusable check API and versioning proposal\\n\\n• Broccoli/template example\\n\\n• Applicability and coverage policy examples\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"B01\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/1aadfce0-343b-4cce-8e87-a04634fdc934.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"development\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Build the independent-column Tasks board\",\"description\":\"Make real inputs and task placements readable and minimally editable.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Inputs / Backlog / Queued / Running / Blocked columns with independent layout.\\n\\n• Root-only backlog, priority groups, selection, breadcrumb and simple persisted create/move actions.\\n\\n• No speculative toolbar or drag-only overlay.\\n\\n• Audit existing table and header components. Reuse/extract header pieces and compose independent column content/scroll; document the chosen shared boundary.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Board is populated from persisted real data, not mockup fixtures.\\n\\n2. Backlog contains only parentless tasks; priorities are ordered 0..n and editable without drag.\\n\\n3. Columns have no common row grid; selection and scroll survive unrelated updates.\\n\\n4. Right side stays blank without a selection, and selected task can open its graph.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Focused board browser tests\\n\\n• Desktop/narrow screenshots\\n\\n• Real create/move/readback demo\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T04\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/1b0e1712-37dd-4821-acdc-ea715b6e3840.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"design\",\"placement\":\"completed\",\"title\":\"Review coherent MVP CRUD images and component coverage\",\"description\":\"Agree a usable complete operation surface before implementing the contextual views.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Apply the full accepted visual direction and latest written corrections; record reusable component/CRUD coverage. Design only, no runtime implementation.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Images plus written requirements cover the agreed board, Node, graph and Review surfaces; missing interactions are explicitly specified rather than claimed from screenshots.\\n\\n2. Operation parity and reusable component boundaries are documented.\\n\\n3. User explicitly accepted the design as good enough, including final small corrections, before development.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Final user annotation message: Make one more generation... I confirm its good enough.\\n\\n• Accepted images and authoritative corrections in imageReview\\n\\n• Component map and acceptance contract\\n\\nExplicit user design acceptance; app behavior remains unimplemented.\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"V01\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/2625b13d-60f6-429a-8510-5ca848cf817b.json\",\"kind\":\"input\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"title\":\"Efficient tool use\",\"description\":\"First, I want to optimize the number of tool calls models have to make to achieve things so :\\r\\n- token usage efficiency improves\\r\\n- time to reach a result improves\\r\\n- reliability and repeatability improve\",\"meaning\":\"user story\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T06:57:45.458Z\",\"capture\":{\"id\":\"71913c2b-a95e-48d9-9556-7293f81ede24\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-24T14:56:10.152Z\",\"history\":[{\"time\":\"2026-09-24T14:56:10.152Z\",\"actor\":\"agent\",\"title\":\"Efficient tool use\",\"description\":\"First, I want to optimize the number of tool calls models have to make to achieve things so :\\r\\n- token usage efficiency improves\\r\\n- time to reach a result improves\\r\\n- reliability and repeatability improve\",\"status\":\"open\"}],\"status\":\"open\",\"type\":\"user story\",\"root\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\vince\\\\Documents\\\\GitHub\\\\Btr\\\\TheBroccoli\",\"title\":\"Efficient tool use\",\"description\":\"First, I want to optimize the number of tool calls models have to make to achieve things so :\\r\\n- token usage efficiency improves\\r\\n- time to reach a result improves\\r\\n- reliability and repeatability improve\",\"context\":{\"kind\":\"source\",\"label\":\"Recorded harness needs\",\"path\":\".runtime/planning/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/harness-effects.md\",\"quote\":\"First, I want to optimize the number of tool calls models have to make to achieve things so :\\r\\n- token usage efficiency improves\\r\\n- time to reach a result improves\\r\\n- reliability and repeatability improve\"}},\"sourceEvidence\":{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/5c26207311aeb27d96e1a828b8515d224253b6da615f4c9c6195768c01f07dc4\",\"hash\":\"5c26207311aeb27d96e1a828b8515d224253b6da615f4c9c6195768c01f07dc4\",\"mime\":\"application/json\",\"size\":9755},\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T06:57:45.459Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/2958350a-14cb-451f-8ff2-c531bd3121dc.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"review\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Review the persisted foundation and tool handoff\",\"description\":\"Verify that data is trustworthy enough to plan the remaining work in it.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Inspect imported records through MCP and the minimal shared human review path from T02 before completion of the new board/graph/Node/Review surfaces.\\n\\n• Exercise CRUD/conflict/restart/delete, owner validation and actor boundaries.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. User can recognize and inspect the real remaining plan.\\n\\n2. The installed plugin exposes working planning operations, safely persists their effects and never starts execution on CRUD.\\n\\n3. Full checkpoint checks pass and an independent agent verifies foundation, MCP and persistence evidence. This delivery gate follows the latest explicit user authorization; no human approval is fabricated. Human-only product actions remain protected.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Imported root/review IDs\\n\\n• Test results and readback demonstration\\n\\n• Independent foundation review outcome\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"R02\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"review\":{\"status\":\"draft\",\"reviewers\":[{\"actorId\":\"agent:independent-foundation-review\",\"required\":true}],\"runnables\":[],\"outcomes\":{},\"target\":null},\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"},{\"id\":\"review\",\"label\":\"Review\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/2a390751-896e-42ae-8f0f-b8310c137ec9.json\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"title\":\"Independent backend foundation review\",\"description\":\"Immutable planning source and design evidence\",\"artifact\":{\"name\":\"Independent backend foundation review\",\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/fa1d2387d3b00f708f6e9ce8b0a06a77d53000a3c00a00dffc7e6fb7a6612e4f\",\"hash\":\"fa1d2387d3b00f708f6e9ce8b0a06a77d53000a3c00a00dffc7e6fb7a6612e4f\",\"mime\":\"text/plain\",\"size\":323},\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"createdBy\":\"system:authorized-bootstrap\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/2aa48dc8-a11b-4a2b-8a49-cc449d56bfcd.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"development\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Expose planning CRUD through relational operations and Broccoli MCP\",\"description\":\"Make the existing contributor/tool architecture the shared operation foundation for agents and UI.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Contributor-owned operation descriptors, Agent usage discovery and existing MCP exposure.\\n\\n• Verify the Broccoli Local plugin can discover/call planning tools in the active composition.\\n\\n• Shared revisions, request IDs, validation, actor identity and deletion/reference semantics.\\n\\n• Expose review requirement configuration and check/result operations through the same owner; verify operation discovery contains the metadata needed by the generic Node view.\\n\\n• Adapt the existing human-operated checkpoint UI using shared controls as the minimum R02 review path: inspect submitted definition/results, create/reply/author-close comments and select own outcome. Bind to the same contributor owner and verified human browser principal; MCP cannot exercise human-only decisions. This small path precedes the full board/Node/Review surfaces and is replaced/composed into them, not duplicated permanently.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Actual Codex MCP tools can create/read/update/delete a disposable task and input; API-only simulation is insufficient.\\n\\n2. UI transport and MCP invoke the same contributor operations and persistence.\\n\\n3. Tool metadata is derived from owner-qualified contracts; no duplicate standalone CLI implementation.\\n\\n4. Stale writes, invalid references and actor impersonation are rejected.\\n\\n5. Before R02, a real human can inspect the submitted planning record and operate closure/outcome controls through the browser. Agent credentials cannot impersonate that user through either MCP or browser transport. A planning-only review does not require code snapshots.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Plugin discovery and live read/write/readback demonstration\\n\\n• MCP/relational operation integration tests\\n\\n• UI/tool contract parity checklist\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T02\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/2af6e80e-9c26-42bb-b095-1ce9dcf7c599.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"integration\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Integrate the surfaces and complete the usage walkthrough\",\"description\":\"Finish a small usable release and remove replaced UI/data paths.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Wire both surfaces, inspector and tools together against the imported real plan.\\n\\n• Remove superseded sample fallback and duplicate old entry points within replaced scope.\\n\\n• Run the acceptance scenario, inspect screenshots and record issues as inputs/tasks.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Every acceptance-scenario step is demonstrated with persisted data.\\n\\n2. The same task edit from MCP appears in UI and UI edit appears in MCP; restart preserves it.\\n\\n3. Replaced code/tests/dependencies are removed without reverting pre-existing unrelated work.\\n\\n4. Full verification passes and screenshot review finds no blocking usability issue.\\n\\n5. Parity is checked operation-by-operation, including deletes, links, priority groups, review actions and import/export.\\n\\n6. Independent implementation review examines actual source, tests and UI; material findings are resolved before handing the running app to the user.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Acceptance walkthrough record\\n\\n• npm run test:all result\\n\\n• Screenshots and linked remaining issues\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T08\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":