ty as possible and the tools to exploit it to further optimize model usage so I can progressively improve AI usage, relying in part on hard evidence.\",\"context\":{\"kind\":\"source\",\"label\":\"Recorded harness needs\",\"path\":\".runtime/planning/01a0c5f4-7593-7072-8985-289e55a9faf9/harness-effects.md\",\"quote\":\"Third, I want to have as much observability as possible and the tools to exploit it to further optimize model usage so I can progressively improve AI usage, relying in part on hard evidence.\"}},\"sourceEvidence\":{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/5c26207311aeb27d96e1a828b8515d224253b6da615f4c9c6195768c01f07dc4\",\"hash\":\"5c26207311aeb27d96e1a828b8515d224253b6da615f4c9c6195768c01f07dc4\",\"mime\":\"application/json\",\"size\":9755},\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T06:57:45.459Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/3370ac45-ec5d-4844-a9e1-a0babee91d50.json\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"title\":\"images/V2-revision-2.png\",\"description\":\"Immutable planning source and design evidence\",\"artifact\":{\"name\":\"images/V2-revision-2.png\",\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/b8c4bab2bd338954ac4993cf6bb7e5c807807b6eb2a263db037b077f48782f15\",\"hash\":\"b8c4bab2bd338954ac4993cf6bb7e5c807807b6eb2a263db037b077f48782f15\",\"mime\":\"image/png\",\"size\":1307807},\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"createdBy\":\"system:authorized-bootstrap\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/381ab975-f064-48d7-ad5e-ab77eac342c8.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"development\",\"placement\":\"running\",\"title\":\"Persist the canonical nested task model\",\"description\":\"Create/edit real title-only plans with durable relations, revisions and history.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Evolve canonical task owner; decouple planning records from execution startup.\\n\\n• Persist inputs, nested tasks, prerequisites, priority groups, attempt/evidence references and actor-attributed events.\\n\\n• Implement transactional validation, stale-write protection and restart recovery.\\n\\n• Resolve active-app/relational-host composition and contributor ownership before storage edits; activate only needed existing dependencies.\\n\\n• Declare field types, relation descriptors (including immutable creator), readable revisions and actor-permitted operation metadata using existing contracts; no ECS migration. Persist review requirements as references to existing check/thread/decision owners.\\n\\n• Implement basic submitted-revision/required-check enforcement, author-owned thread closure and authenticated outcome transitions before R02. Read-model/evidence refinements remain T07; do not defer fundamental gate enforcement until then.\\n\\n• Implement review draft/readiness transition and distinct continuation task relations, immutable multi-repository submitted evidence and grouped-feedback persistence; retain the existing canonical owners.\\n\\n• Reuse existing decentralized graph serialization/identity contracts and verify persisted references resolve correctly after full deserialization and restart. Do not create a second link encoding or URL UI feature.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Title-only tasks and multi-level nesting survive restart without starting/scanning an execution workspace.\\n\\n2. Cycles, missing references, invalid cross-context links and stale writes are rejected without partial mutation.\\n\\n3. Reversible placements and dynamic priority groups preserve history and never start an agent.\\n\\n4. No second planning-task authority is introduced.\\n\\n5. UI and MCP reach one owner/store through explicit relational contracts, not cross-project source imports or parallel task copies.\\n\\n6. Review requirements and revisions have one owner; Node/Review and UI/MCP cannot disagree through duplicate derived state.\\n\\n7. Draft/submitted/blocked/changes-requested/passed/abandoned transitions enforce the documented freeze and gate rules. A rejected review cannot strand its dependants: explicit validated successor gate replacement enables them only after the new review passes, preserving old evidence and comments.\\n\\n8. Work continuation creation and later draft review creation are separately idempotent; retry duplicates neither node nor relation and future review evidence is not fabricated.\\n\\n9. Serialize a graph with nested/shared references, review targets, discussion anchors, evidence revisions and successor links; discard in-memory state and deserialize/restart under a changed runtime binding. Every resolvable link reaches the same logical target, shared identity is preserved, and missing targets remain explicit unresolved references rather than retargeted or dropped.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Focused domain/storage tests\\n\\n• Failure/restart readback\\n\\n• Storage ownership note\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T01\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/397de05d-5d0a-4016-b631-24fd7319b540.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"review\",\"placement\":\"completed\",\"title\":\"Review the MVP foundation and scope\",\"description\":\"Agree the smallest useful contract before implementation.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Final plan-only review converged after two clean-context rounds and recorded dispositions.\\n\\n• Visual design is accepted, final annotations recorded, URL UI deferred, and persisted-link requirements clarified; no unresolved user questions remain.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. The plan specifies the same owning planning operations for UI and existing MCP, with acceptance tests assigned; actual operation availability is verified at R02/R03, not claimed before implementation.\\n\\n2. User has reviewed the contextual CRUD images and component plan.\\n\\n3. No unresolved comments or decisions remain; approval is recorded.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Reviewed plan revision/hash\\n\\n• User comments and explicit outcome\\n\\nPlanning/design approval only, recorded from user instructions and final clarification; no application implementation is claimed.\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"R01\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"review\":{\"status\":\"passed\",\"reviewers\":[{\"actorId\":\"human:user\",\"required\":true}],\"runnables\":[],\"outcomes\":{\"human:user\":{\"value\":\"approved\",\"historical\":true,\"source\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/b9789e157fd8192bc63f9dbd7035f11b93c2c426d1c173b4aeedb530159a99de\",\"reason\":\"User explicitly accepted the design and development direction, requested final plan review and resolution of remaining questions; the independent review converged, and the latest user message resolves the only remaining question by deferring URL UI.\"}},\"target\":{\"revision\":1,\"nodes\":{},\"sessions\":[],\"historicalSource\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/b9789e157fd8192bc63f9dbd7035f11b93c2c426d1c173b4aeedb530159a99de\"}},\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"},{\"id\":\"review\",\"label\":\"Review\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/4b6e5329-6df7-485e-8296-8b32c09d6e48.json\",\"kind\":\"input\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"t