2d67fa84.json\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"title\":\"PLAN.md\",\"description\":\"Immutable planning source and design evidence\",\"artifact\":{\"name\":\"PLAN.md\",\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/b155cce8e971482ecee563ae3d28316effb9570cdd6b523371be297107fc6f06\",\"hash\":\"b155cce8e971482ecee563ae3d28316effb9570cdd6b523371be297107fc6f06\",\"mime\":\"text/markdown\",\"size\":120978},\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"createdBy\":\"system:authorized-bootstrap\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/8c71b1d4-590b-4529-8120-e95713107b64.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"integration\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Connect real evidence and review gates\",\"description\":\"Make review and observation work with actual results rather than sample content.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Reuse session/turn-range, current diff, captured snapshot and check-run evidence.\\n\\n• Review ordinary tasks against definitions/results or exact code snapshots; support blocked/revise/approve/abandon outcomes.\\n\\n• Keep reviewed scope frozen, block dependants and preserve independent work choices.\\n\\n• Project automatic/semantic/deterministic requirements and author-owned comment closure into a unified review check collection; requirement provenance and submitted revision are retained.\\n\\n• Build on the basic gate enforcement delivered in T01/T02 for R02; integrate richer file/session/check evidence and unified presentation without creating a second owner.\\n\\n• Detect/aggregate existing repository-owned checks and wire one granular run-checks operation through shared UI/MCP; attach existing coverage/report evidence without building the shared-check framework.\\n\\n• Adapt freshness gates so the human can explicitly accept an earlier passed run for the selected revision; show both the mismatch and acceptance, never a fabricated fresh pass.\\n\\n• Wire header run-all/mandatory/selected and scoped cancellation to the shared check owner; preserve partial evidence and distinguish unsupported cancellation.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Planning-only review does not require a fake Git diff or code checks.\\n\\n2. Code review shows the exact submitted revision and run provenance. Stale results are flagged and block passage unless the human records target-specific acceptance of earlier passed evidence; changed snapshot identity is never silently substituted.\\n\\n3. All comments must close and all required reviewers approve; generic edits cannot bypass gates.\\n\\n4. Sessions may span attempts via turn ranges; evidence links open the correct existing viewer.\\n\\n5. Shared checkout limits are visible, without falsely promising automatic parallel isolation.\\n\\n6. Reviewer decisions and comment/input closure derive from their owners. Generic metadata changes cannot manufacture passage; open comments remain blocking. Stale passed evidence can be accepted only by an explicit human decision bound to the target revision.\\n\\n7. One run-checks call resolves repository-owned applicable checks at the requested granularity and aggregates their results without requiring the agent to choose individual commands.\\n\\n8. Execution record distinguishes selected/run/skipped/not-run checks, versions and when each ran. Later changes preserve the old result and reveal the mismatch.\\n\\n9. Coverage exposes measured result and effective threshold with available scope/provenance. No line/file/function coverage explorer, shared pipeline engine or agent-review harness is required.\\n\\n10. All/mandatory/selected deduplicate runnable targets and never invoke reviewer/closure rows. Stop records affected run IDs and observed cancellation/partial results; cancelled/missing evidence never becomes mandatory pass.\\n\\n11. Latest nested check evidence and chronological run events reference the same stored execution; neither rewrites policy or hides stale results.\\n\\n12. Failed-R02 replacement scenario passes end to end, including required-actor finish boundary, overlapping freeze protection, unresolved comment carry-forward and no generic-unlink gate bypass.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Review/evidence integration tests\\n\\n• Blocked-dependant and snapshot mismatch demonstrations\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T07\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/8f1bb153-b9b8-42f6-b333-107c077fe2b4.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"integration\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Import this plan and transfer authority to app data\",\"description\":\"Start using persisted app planning before finishing the visual surfaces.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• One-time dry-run/apply importer with source ID mapping and receipt.\\n\\n• Import tasks/dependencies/review gates and all approved global requirements and visual corrections. Preserve goals/criteria in descriptions and the complete source with image assets as immutable app-owned evidence; only genuinely completed history is imported.\\n\\n• Readback, restart, retry and temporary-document retirement.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Every bootstrap task, goal, criterion, dependency and review gate matches persisted readback.\\n\\n2. Failed import is atomic; repeated import creates no duplicates or execution.\\n\\n3. Receipt identifies the root and all app IDs; remaining updates use app tools.\\n\\n4. Bootstrap planning details are replaced by the receipt/link after verification.\\n\\n5. Complete approved specification, annotated images and source snapshot are retrievable from the app after bootstrap retirement/restart, with hash-verified evidence; no parallel editable plan remains.\\n\\n6. Import/readback/restart preserves all serialized graph link identities and immutable target references through the existing format; resolution does not depend on an old runtime port or object instance.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• Import receipt and source hash\\n\\n• Readback/restart comparison\\n\\n• One real task update through MCP\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T03\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/8f584e9a-cb8f-4cd9-8735-fdd76e814b8c.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"development\",\"placement\":\"backlog\",\"title\":\"Compose complete UI CRUD and review controls\",\"description\":\"Let the user perform every supported planning operation independently through reusable UI components.\\n\\nScope\\n\\n• Implement every UI/MCP parity row using existing controls, targeted rework and approved shared additions.\\n\\n• Use the reviewed V1-V4 layouts for task/input relationships, queue/state actions, evidence and review.\\n\\n• Include create/delete, link/unlink, priorities, import/export and structured conflict/error handling.\\n\\n• Implement schema/reflection-driven Node view and one view matching adapter over existing types/fields/relations.\\n\\n• Reuse persisted graph-reference resolution and existing navigation; implement node revision comparison with shared controls. New URL UI is excluded.\\n\\n• Compose shared Review tabs, Author readiness, grouped-feedback display/composer, single-column Checks hierarchy and shared selection/toolbar components. Integrate existing files/diff/Preview views without custom substitutes.\\n\\nSuccess criteria\\n\\n1. Every exposed planning tool operation has a tested, discoverable UI path; no routine operation requires Codex or hand-edited JSON.\\n\\n2. UI and MCP use identical owning operation contracts and actor-specific restrictions.\\n\\n3. No surface-specific form, selector, command menu, thread widget or graph renderer duplicates a reusable component.\\n\\n4. Unselected panel is blank; keyboard/focus/draft behavior survives unrelated updates.\\n\\n5. Node works for editable and read-only nodes; creator is a read-only relation. No schema-specific task screen duplicates the shared renderer.\\n\\n6. Node and evidence navigation resolve deserialized graph links to the correct target/revision using existing contracts; missing/deleted targets are explicit. No new URL UI or external browser-entry acceptance requirement.\\n\\n7. No/inline/side-by-side comparison handles fields and relations. Historical read-only selection never changes expectedRevision for live writes.\\n\\n8. Review has Overview/Changes/Preview, Author readiness and Checks -> Reviewers/Runnables -> Mandatory/Optional. Four right-aligned Runnables tree-row actions operate highlights; no checkboxes, per-item play controls, duplicate outcome/action panels or URL strip.\\n\\n9. Both new comments and replies use the same editable typed-row component with row removal, clear boundaries and bottom actions; top-level content spans available width and replies alone indent.\\n\\n10. Changes exposes all/modified files and exact target/composed iteration diff, line-anchored feedback and Preview reuse; view switching preserves unrelated panel state.\\n\\n11. Runnables is an ordinary nested row under Checks; the Overview inner splitter begins below the toolbar and every far-right view tool remains inside the toolbar spanning both subpanes.\\n\\nEvidence\\n\\n• UI/MCP parity acceptance matrix\\n\\n• V1-V4 browser screenshots\\n\\n• Independent user CRUD walkthrough\\n\\n\",\"importSource\":\"planning-review-mvp\",\"sourceKey\":\"T06\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.292Z\",\"createdBy\":\"agent:codex\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"},{\"id\":\"graph\",\"label\":\"Graph\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/actor-agent-codex.json\",\"kind\":\"actor\",\"context\":null,\"title\":\"Codex\",\"actorId\":\"agent:codex\",\"actorKind\":\"agent\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/actor-system-authorized-bootstrap.json\",\"kind\":\"actor\",\"context\":null,\"title\":\"Approved planning handoff\",\"actorId\":\"system:authorized-bootstrap\",\"actorKind\":\"system\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/b48cbd5b-cc13-4a97-8dfb-7c437fb77213.json\",\"kind\":\"evidence\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"title\":\"images/V4-revision-2.png\",\"description\":\"Immutable planning source and design evidence\",\"artifact\":{\"name\":\"images/V4-revision-2.png\",\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/evidence/59e6fd07a59de6ec0e0c27afb1a2edb893861b27eb8d3a187f9db79959ef3069\",\"hash\":\"59e6fd07a59de6ec0e0c27afb1a2edb893861b27eb8d3a187f9db79959ef3069\",\"mime\":\"image/png\",\"size\":1583275},\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-09-27T07:49:03.293Z\",\"createdBy\":\"system:authorized-bootstrap\",\"views\":[{\"id\":\"node\",\"label\":\"Node\"}]},{\"id\":\"graph://planning-26535745-4644-4770-af7c-1980c773377b/entries/b607a592-b883-4ad3-925d-61e9774fc201.json\",\"kind\":\"task\",\"context\":\"99a62c14-535f-4d9a-9ab2-642ed280b795\",\"purpose\":\"review\",\"placement\":\"completed\",\"title\":\"Review the software implementation design\",\"description\":\"Resolve ownership, storage, components and ve